kdp:prompts.text:
Give me 10 romantasy trilogy concepts using these genres, tropes and themes:

GENRES: {{GENRES}}
TROPES: {{TROPES}}
THEMES: {{THEMES}}
ROMANCE ARC: {{ROMANCE_ARC}}

For each: a one-line logline, the central bargain, and what makes book II different from book I.

Here is my story dossier:

{{DOSSIER}}

Critique it purely on EMOTION. Where will a reader feel nothing? Which turns are intellectually clever but emotionally inert? Name the three moments that must hit hardest and say whether the dossier earns them.

Original dossier:
{{DOSSIER}}

Emotional critique:
{{EMOTIONAL_CRITIQUE}}

Name critiques:
{{NAME_CRITIQUES}}

Rewrite the dossier resolving every critique. Keep the premise. Change nothing that was working.

Fill this character sheet for {{CHARACTER_NAME}}, the {{ROLE}} of {{TRILOGY}}.

Story dossier for context:
{{DOSSIER}}

Sheet:
{{CHARACTER_SHEET_TEMPLATE}}

The wound and the lie must explain the arc. No generic answers.

Worldbuilding element: {{ELEMENT}}
Trilogy: {{TRILOGY}}
Dossier: {{DOSSIER}}

Build it with: summary, hard rules, limits and cost, how it appears on the page, and the three contradictions I must never write.

Outline {{BOOK_TITLE}} chapter by chapter — 40 chapters, Act I ch 1–10, Act II ch 11–30, Act III ch 31–40.

Dossier: {{DOSSIER}}
Characters: {{CHARACTERS}}
World: {{WORLD}}

Use this template per chapter:
{{CHAPTER_OUTLINE_TEMPLATE}}

Write Chapter {{CHAPTER_NO}} of {{BOOK_TITLE}}.

Outline:
{{CHAPTER_OUTLINE}}

POV: {{POV_CHARACTER}}
Prior beat: {{PREVIOUS_CHAPTER_END}}
Style sheet: {{STYLE_SHEET}}
Sample prose to match: {{SAMPLE_PROSE}}
Never use: {{FORBIDDEN_WORDS}}

Target 3,000–3,400 words. End on the turn, not the aftermath.

Here is chapter {{CHAPTER_NO}}:

{{CHAPTER_TEXT}}

Produce an improvement plan — not a rewrite. Cover: where tension slackens, dialogue that states the subtext, description that stalls the scene, the romance beat landing or not, and whether the exit line earns the page turn.

Original chapter:
{{CHAPTER_TEXT}}

Improvement plan:
{{IMPROVEMENT_PLAN}}

Rewrite the chapter applying every point. Keep what already worked. Match: {{STYLE_SHEET}}. Never use: {{FORBIDDEN_WORDS}}.

Line edit this chapter. Tighten sentences, cut filter words, vary rhythm, strengthen verbs. Do not change events, dialogue meaning, or voice.

{{CHAPTER_TEXT}}

Forbidden words: {{FORBIDDEN_WORDS}}

Write an Amazon KDP blurb for {{BOOK_TITLE}}.

Logline: {{LOGLINE}}
Tropes: {{TROPES}}
Comp titles: {{COMPS}}

Hook in the first line. Under 200 words. End on the question, not the answer.

Give me 7 Amazon KDP keyword phrases and 3 categories for:

{{BOOK_TITLE}} — {{LOGLINE}}
Tropes: {{TROPES}}

Keywords must be phrases readers actually search, not single words. Explain each in six words.
